      "title": "packet-tls-utils:Avoid calling ssl_hmac_init() and ssl_hmac_cleanup() in a loop",
      "message": "packet-tls-utils:Avoid calling ssl_hmac_init() and ssl_hmac_cleanup() in a loop\n\nInstead of calling ssl_hmac_init() and ssl_hmac_cleanup() in\na loop, call ssl_hmac_reset(), to avoid creating and releasing\ncontexts. This should also fix Coverity 1450768, which\ndetects the multiple calls to ssl_hmac_final() as a double-free.\n",
      "author_name": "Moshe Kaplan",
      "author_email": "me@moshekaplan.com",
      "authored_date": "2020-11-27T00:09:02.000-05:00",
      "committer_name": "Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
